question-capture/14041191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{7}^{1/3}≈\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041191/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bc04b4fa828f49d63d514301685b90ac2d3c8a5d8d4d717f2c6bee719f96386" "basis" 1484 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{7}^{1/3}≈\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041191/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bc04b4fa828f49d63d514301685b90ac2d3c8a5d8d4d717f2c6bee719f96386" "basis" 1484 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $\\sqrt{x}$ about $x=4$ to approximate the value of $\\sqrt{\\pi }.$ Give your answer to $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0df9c60fbfa50c1407a0a86e63aba915a56ae530ee7d7b2a5c5ab3b12314555" "basis" 1767 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=4.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt{x}={x}^{1/2} \\\\ f(4) & ={4}^{1/2}=2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(4) & =-\\frac{1}{4}(4)^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{{2}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & =2+\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}(x-4)-\\frac{1}{2!}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{5}})(x-4)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =2+\\frac{x-4}{4}-\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{64}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\pi $ into the above to approximate $\\sqrt{\\pi }.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } & ≈2+\\frac{\\pi -4}{4}-\\frac{(\\pi -4)^{2}}{64} \\\\  & =1.773\\,9\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0df9c60fbfa50c1407a0a86e63aba915a56ae530ee7d7b2a5c5ab3b12314555" "basis" 1767 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "855a329f75d6c9547335789135af70b608d40f74a828b15a6737ce119f20c439" "basis" 1767 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0df9c60fbfa50c1407a0a86e63aba915a56ae530ee7d7b2a5c5ab3b12314555" "basis" 1767 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052556/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value"